spes: countdown back to fastboot (spesautofb=N minutes) and DSP shutdown before a reset (0207).

User's idea: a test boot should never run forever. spesautofb=N starts a thread that logs the countdown and after N
minutes does what the USB "fastboot" command does (PON reason with read-back, bounded syncs, IMEM, PSCI reset); the reset
path is now one function ud_reset() shared by both. all-5: the reset happened with the modem and ADSP up but fastboot never
appeared; Linux stops its remoteprocs on reboot, so ud_reset() now asks TrustZone for PAS shutdown of the modem (if it was
booted) and the ADSP first (spes_dsps_shutdown in SpesModem.cpp).

